---
metaTitle: Submissions | How to send coins for grading
metaDescription: 'How to submit coins: request a quote, pack each coin securely, ship insured, and receive your coins graded, sealed and on record.'
eyebrow: Submissions
heading: Sending coins to us.
intro: Every submission begins with a short conversation about what you would like to send. Nothing needs to be shipped until you have our quote.
sections:
  - mark: attribute
    title: Tell us what you would like to send
    text: Use the submission request below, or contact us directly. A list of the coins, a rough idea of their value and the service you have in mind are enough to begin. If you are unsure which service suits a coin, say so and we will advise.
  - mark: registry
    title: Receive your quote
    text: We reply with a quote for your submission and the address to ship to. Turnaround depends on the service and is given with your quote; it is an estimate, not a guarantee.
  - mark: intake
    title: Pack with care
    text: Good packing protects your coins on the way to us.
    points:
      - Place each coin in its own soft, inert holder or flip. Never tape a coin directly.
      - Pad the coins so nothing can move or rub, and use a sturdy box rather than a padded envelope.
      - Enclose a copy of your submission, with your name and contact details.
      - Please do not mix Greek and Roman coins on one invoice.
  - mark: seal
    title: Ship insured
    text: Coins travel at the sender's risk until they reach us, so we recommend insurance. Signature delivery is required for orders valued over $750.
  - mark: return
    title: Graded, sealed and returned
    text: Each coin is authenticated, attributed, graded and sealed, then entered in our certificate registry and returned to you by tracked mail.
feesEyebrow: Fees
feesTitle: Fees and submissions
feesText: |-
  Grading fees depend on the coin and on the service it needs, so we do not publish a single price list. Each submission is quoted individually, before anything is sent.

  If you would like to see our work first, a small trial submission is welcome.
feesLink: Ask for a quote
requestEyebrow: Submission request
requestTitle: Tell us about your coins.
requestText: We reply with a quote and shipping details. Nothing needs to be sent until then.
---
